WEBVTT

00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:03.480
Meet Fizz: the physical layer for AI agents.

00:00:04.900 --> 00:00:08.543
AI agents can write code, plan trips, and answer almost anything.

00:00:08.593 --> 00:00:10.872
But they are blind to the physical world.

00:00:10.922 --> 00:00:14.906
They can't tell you the basement is flooding, the garage air is unsafe,

00:00:14.956 --> 00:00:16.952
or the server closet is overheating.

00:00:17.002 --> 00:00:21.440
That data is stuck in separate apps and dashboards that nobody watches at 3 AM.

00:00:22.300 --> 00:00:26.843
Fizz gives your agent senses. Connect any sensor, ask about it in plain English,

00:00:26.893 --> 00:00:30.230
and get a phone call the moment something crosses the line.

00:00:31.800 --> 00:00:37.107
Sign up with a username and a six-digit code. Then choose what Fizz should sense:

00:00:37.157 --> 00:00:41.737
water, gas, radio, temperature, pressure, humidity, sound, your phone,

00:00:41.787 --> 00:00:44.977
or a custom metric. One click starts sample data,

00:00:45.027 --> 00:00:47.160
so you see it working right away.

00:00:47.700 --> 00:00:53.080
Every sensor streams to a live dashboard, labeled simulated, live API, or phone.

00:00:54.200 --> 00:00:57.174
Now just talk to Fizz. Ask what the temperature is,

00:00:57.224 --> 00:01:01.740
and it answers from your stored readings, citing the sensor, value, and time.

00:01:02.800 --> 00:01:05.403
Then set a watch. Pick a sensor and a threshold,

00:01:05.453 --> 00:01:09.880
and choose whether Fizz should just show it on the dashboard, or call your phone.

00:01:11.200 --> 00:01:16.075
To connect real hardware, switch a sensor to API mode. It gets its own key,

00:01:16.125 --> 00:01:19.425
shown once and revocable. Then it's one HTTPS call.

00:01:19.475 --> 00:01:24.350
Post a reading above the limit, and the database fires the alert instantly.

00:01:27.900 --> 00:01:30.850
Ask Fizz, and it knows exactly what happened.

00:01:33.800 --> 00:01:38.375
No hardware? Send a pairing link to any phone. It shares motion, location,

00:01:38.425 --> 00:01:41.375
and voice notes, each behind its own permission,

00:01:41.425 --> 00:01:43.500
and Fizz can recall what you said.

00:01:48.700 --> 00:01:54.129
Fizz is built with Rust on Vercel, Supabase, Vercel AI Gateway, and AgentPhone.

00:01:54.179 --> 00:01:58.290
Give your AI agent a body. Try Fizz at fizzlayer.com.

